 "text": "..title\nA resolution to amend Ordinance No. BL2026-1244 to authorize The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to modify the acceptance of new public water and sanitary sewer mains and easements, for two properties located at 3124 Murfreesboro Pike and 3201 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Antioch 15 Phase 1, (MWS Project Nos. 25-WL-46 and 25-SL-110 and Proposal No. 2025M-183ES-002).\n..body\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2026-1244, approved, February 19, 2026, authorized the acceptance of approximately 2,396 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,992 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,217 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four fire hydrant assemblies, 20 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for two properties located at 3124 Murfreesboro Pike and 3201 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Antioch 15 Phase 1 and,\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 75 fewer linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC) and approximately 106 fewer linear feet of eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), and the vertical realignment of the water main, are now needed to construct Project Nos. 25-WL-46 and 25-SL-110; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2022M-183ES-002 on April 10, 2026, for revisions to the original mandatory referral; and,\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2026-1244 provides that amendments to the legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nNow, therefore, be it resolved by the Council of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County:\nSection 1.\tThat Ordinance No. BL2026-1244 is hereby amended by deleting Section 1 in its entirety and replacing it with the following:\nThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 2,401 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,917 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,111 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four fire hydrant assemblies, 20 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for two properties located at 3124 Murfreesboro Pike and 3201 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Antioch 15 Phase 1- Revision 1, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n16400004200\t\t\t\t\t3124 Murfreesboro Pike\n15000012500\t\t\t\t\t3201 Hamilton Church Road\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this resolution. \nSection 3. This resolution shall take effect upon passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution amends Ordinance No. BL2026-1244, which was approved by the Metropolitan Council on February 19, 2026. The ordinance authorized the acceptance of approximately 2,396 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,992 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,217 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four fire hydrant assemblies, 20 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for two properties located at 3124 Murfreesboro Pike and 3201 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Antioch 15 Phase 1.\n\nThe proposed resolution would amend Ordinance No. BL2026-1244, to accept approximately 75 fewer linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC) and approximately 106 fewer linear feet of eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP) and accepts a vertical realignment of the water main.\n\nThis amendment has been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\n"
